  measured : median_width_frames = 1.98; p10 = 1.1; p90 = 3.73; step_deg = 0.2; width_deg_upper_estimate = 0.3954; n = 3937
  rule     : note when the median spot width is below 3 frames (undersampled profile) or above 30 frames (oversampled). (median spot width in frames below which the profile is sampled by fewer than about 3 frames (A39: median 1.3-2.4 at 0.2 deg))
  evidence : spots.omega_width_frames (the blob's extent in frames) of the blobs behind the observations
  do       : a finer rotation step would resolve the profile: as a rule of thumb about a quarter of the spot width, here roughly 0.0989 deg (with a proportionally shorter exposure per frame); the total dose and scan time stay the same
