[NOTE] rotation range shorter than 180 deg: few or no in-run Friedel pairs  (scan_range)
  measured : per_run = {'r02': {'range_deg': 170.0, 'pairs_predicted': 150, 'pairs_observed': 38}, 'r03': {'range_deg': 170.0, 'pairs_predicted': 151, 'pairs_observed': 57}, 'r04': {'range_deg': 170.0, 'pairs_predicted': 154, 'pairs_observed': 47}}; short_runs = ['r02', 'r03', 'r04']; pairs_predicted_360deg_same_orientation = 925; geometry_refined_from_data = True; fewest_in_run_pairs_in_short_runs = 38; cross_run = {'signed_hkl_with_mate_in_another_run': 1802, 'signed_hkl_observed': 3120}
  rule     : range < 180 deg means (almost) no in-run Friedel pairs; limiting only if the geometry was refined from the data AND fewer than 30 in-run pairs exist and the range is not set by the sample environment
  evidence : run.geom (omega_step, n_frames), predicted_crossings of all expected signed hkl with the run's refined U and geometry (pairs = unordered {h,-h} both crossing), run.obs for observed pairs
  do       : Scan at least 180 deg (360 deg if the sample environment allows): every reflection then has its Friedel mate in the same run, which gives an estimate of the detector tilt tx and the rotation-axis wedge that does not depend on the orientation fit, plus an internal check of absorption/centring. Not urgent here: 38 in-run pairs (fewest over the short runs) exist, enough to check the fitted wedge/tilts (at least 30); a longer scan would still make the check complete.
  gain     : simulated (validation/real/PREREG_friedel_geometry.md, positive control): about 1500 pairs of a 360 deg scan give tx +-0.002 deg and wedge +-0.001 deg; about 100 pairs give +-0.01 deg. On the real L-alanine runs (170 deg, 35-57 in-run pairs) the pair estimates agreed with the orientation fit within 0.035 deg (INCONCLUSIVE by the registered rule).
  not covered: Predicted pair counts are geometric (a crossing on the detector); observed counts are what survived integration. Pairs between different runs need the unknown relative rotation of the runs and are reported, not used.

